WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.375
Click the parts button in the repair list.

00:00:02.375 --> 00:00:06.125
The window already contains the repair items chosen at intake.

00:00:06.125 --> 00:00:09.333
Fill in each item without creating the same item again.

00:00:09.333 --> 00:00:12.250
Use the supplier field for items you need to buy.

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:13.625
A quote is optional.

00:00:13.625 --> 00:00:16.917
Purchase cost is editable only with financial permission.

00:00:16.917 --> 00:00:20.042
A quote without a supplier does not create a purchase.

00:00:20.042 --> 00:00:22.833
Review the quote and supplier, then save.

00:00:22.833 --> 00:00:25.000
The item remains pending purchase.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:30.125
The website does not place orders; the customer quote and
internal cost stay separate.

00:00:30.125 --> 00:00:34.625
After ordering from the supplier, open the corresponding
purchase record.

00:00:34.625 --> 00:00:40.625
Explicitly confirm that the order was actually placed, then
record that fact for each item separately.

00:00:40.625 --> 00:00:46.792
Open batch arrivals, choose the supplier and items, then enter
the quantities received in this delivery.

00:00:46.792 --> 00:00:48.042
Review and save.

00:00:48.042 --> 00:00:50.375
Record separate deliveries separately.

00:00:50.375 --> 00:00:54.042
The purchase page shows received quantities and linked repairs.

00:00:54.042 --> 00:00:58.833
When parts arrive, still update the repair and contact the
customer as appropriate.

00:00:58.833 --> 00:01:01.167
These records are not parts inventory.
